{
  "description": "Identity `claims` is modeled as an object with only `aud` and `sub`, but Doppler validates any claim an identity configures: \"Audience and subject claims are required. Additional custom claims can be added as desired\", keyed by claim name or by a JSON Pointer for nested claims (https://docs.doppler.com/docs/service-account-identities). The Terraform provider sends and reads claims as map<string, string[]> (DopplerHQ/terraform-provider-doppler doppler/models.go:362-379). Separately, the create response nests ttl_seconds, created_at and last_seen_at under `config`, while the get and update responses in the same spec, and the Terraform provider's identity model, put them on the identity itself. `last_seen_at` is null until the identity is first used, as it is for service account tokens (the token create example's `last_seen_at` is null) and for GET /v3/me (live, 2026-10-13).",
